[{:db/id "q-117798/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "2a5bdf80-8c20-5542-afe4-efdc648d57e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "c7f1433a-d16c-5912-b99a-14916f963a18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "5177fa95-c1d1-5de1-8121-d1d408813501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e1eb8646-9cc3-597e-953d-548a532e11a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "b0b6253c-9462-5455-9855-2849b9b0b77c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "95bc63e3-9e9b-5b36-9517-c8f886b958a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117798/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer-field/choices ["q-117798/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" "q-117798/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-117798/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-117798/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-117798/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117798" :question/id #uuid "7b5e1232-2af8-533d-8946-1db7e40dfb1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-117798" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/454c2746d17f6444a9fa5762baae3927fb72eff6a7e51a1df38bc4f325a4a830.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-0=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})}=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $2$ units up. Hence, $D=2.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{3}{2}+2=\\frac{7}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2})+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117798/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117798"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection/92a29462ba5dcee0dd5ac84d013d7fc790518cbaa8e5b5d71bb4beb2d088b16e" :answer/id #uuid "7d1b4101-040d-556b-8e44-e33c2ec32457" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection/168c4d08400d1780c78bb8b80e10dff36395aaaad9d170e2d9594f356953759c" :answer/id #uuid "7f31a8bd-9acc-54ef-b171-104cab111adf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection/1cec20ab2e4b6577f1ce1ab31ae7518dfcadda99dabd4191113bed24aa33e94f" :answer/id #uuid "80195f7c-9a2e-5881-a561-0d8f50a04f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection/922a5499bd89b001cbc292517b8c94f994612b55b26083c0b5e899dce750b611" :answer/id #uuid "8589059f-f1bc-5cdd-aec4-578ae120d44c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection/df0a02eee36ca5d9f8ef916941b9f30bd0840177cc79b5ea94ec34b1671c0f53" :answer/id #uuid "c303bbe2-0895-57af-8693-7a06d3d34564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29f671bf-57cb-597c-8402-bd70656d18fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117888/selection/df0a02eee36ca5d9f8ef916941b9f30bd0840177cc79b5ea94ec34b1671c0f53" :answer-field/choices ["q-117888/selection/92a29462ba5dcee0dd5ac84d013d7fc790518cbaa8e5b5d71bb4beb2d088b16e" "q-117888/selection/168c4d08400d1780c78bb8b80e10dff36395aaaad9d170e2d9594f356953759c" "q-117888/selection/1cec20ab2e4b6577f1ce1ab31ae7518dfcadda99dabd4191113bed24aa33e94f" "q-117888/selection/922a5499bd89b001cbc292517b8c94f994612b55b26083c0b5e899dce750b611" "q-117888/selection/df0a02eee36ca5d9f8ef916941b9f30bd0840177cc79b5ea94ec34b1671c0f53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117888" :question/id #uuid "6101e7db-17ef-5f41-b6aa-dedb998ac867" :question/math-academy-id "q-117888" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/5819e0605dacfb190c2767c4f50a671eb592832aa6a3a1970a8bcdff2790fd19.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{3}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3(x+\\frac{C}{3}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/ad5bf0001a37cf5bebf3288ffbf1fa6bb69747f28f8a81d08d0ffab8223e1707.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x)$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{21}-0=\\frac{\\pi }{21}$ units to the right. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{3}=-\\frac{\\pi }{21}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{7}.\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{7}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $-\\frac{\\pi }{7}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117888/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117888"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection/42d84e4a0457035d14dfcae2406dc9405241c35bc79e6c69f43f243d88fd8bc7" :answer/id #uuid "90ed00e1-1f2f-5683-bc81-f6670ac548d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection/8d714c1fd416e58da765395a7a57c526e1b97a45c41a59520f74d433a1e9ba87" :answer/id #uuid "0f1cb54b-2ac8-5046-ad4a-07cb6479bbc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "35712184-4acb-5776-8445-4bc98d8c9b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "4a8ffaae-da7e-535a-9cc5-ea8f3f208dc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0" :answer/id #uuid "487b38bc-ff16-52d2-aa97-b5843ab8b967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3f3631-d87b-5f00-8744-a6c4890e026d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117891/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-117891/selection/42d84e4a0457035d14dfcae2406dc9405241c35bc79e6c69f43f243d88fd8bc7" "q-117891/selection/8d714c1fd416e58da765395a7a57c526e1b97a45c41a59520f74d433a1e9ba87" "q-117891/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-117891/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" "q-117891/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117891" :question/id #uuid "52dd95a7-09e4-56b0-895f-efb86e073bb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117891" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/4374d7ede23ffbb78ed861d8ebdf116126c546490a87771505cfbe121b973247.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/cac3ea6b8409290b6716a194325a885672e06572c1f8a8b63b48b6807f514d42.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)$ by $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ units to the left. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,⟹\\,C=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117891/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer/id #uuid "a64e72d4-2879-518d-9201-979fab7adaab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "97ef6dd8-4c5b-5809-9122-4f24c7e9f343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "5b2dd5e5-8108-59f7-8094-2d139667eb3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection/671723d87f1a67d9aa6a1f954b934e271d81eedfb75a65037fca3403ebebfd96" :answer/id #uuid "b65f0fbf-db07-5593-ab33-61d4f6a2c48e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e" :answer/id #uuid "d48bad41-6151-5d6d-b552-122ed5656569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8ec1bad-0938-5980-8f74-c9e1b9eeb5f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143669/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" :answer-field/choices ["q-143669/selection/bd79c0c06aebc779b7361f220b7135833ae30fce981dac621db59a8b51d52f52" "q-143669/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-143669/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-143669/selection/671723d87f1a67d9aa6a1f954b934e271d81eedfb75a65037fca3403ebebfd96" "q-143669/selection/b8fe8d3cb42910de21f3df8634e1c373223a74d32bfef959cca9ceacd5c4d03e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143669" :question/id #uuid "d39218d1-1972-5152-bee8-516235be3a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-143669" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/f86984919b15283134e1b3a9479ff8c79ec8dfacc84975e82f88704b7b26dd3a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is  $B-2D?$" :question/worked-solution "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{cot}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=4.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the cotangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{9}{4}$ unit down. Therefore, $D=-\\frac{9}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, $B-2D=4-2\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{4})=4+\\frac{9}{2}=\\frac{17}{2}.$  \n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(4x)-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143669/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dac9c72b-c23f-56fa-b939-6e3b56d3a13b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "c928ce5d-6010-56a5-8954-c3d527c31793" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer/id #uuid "465cedd5-61d4-5236-a50b-1af25be79599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0" :answer/id #uuid "b1a99b1e-a904-5335-9e57-816a9d712f71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "7727bc6e-9b39-532a-8f01-16f7a9967077" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "193a4cb1-7db9-56fe-a1d2-d4f205ae130b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd2223db-c1d3-583f-b0bf-26ceecc64031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143671/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-143671/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" "q-143671/selection/75d4bf82dfc61c34c77bbbf7bd5b3bd55806108bbef22fc9bcd32571f4f3b0b8" "q-143671/selection/09e535b811e1e7584404784c7ac4f577a3ed9805710046fc8fb895ffb3de13a0" "q-143671/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-143671/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143671" :question/id #uuid "05c8c3e7-eede-5ba7-84d2-9182c0468743" :question/math-academy-id "q-143671" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/b29154c183a57397bba6050ad02e543ad47e4b979c77435c9f6e88a49e32783e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x+C),$ where $C$ is a constant. Given that $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ what is the value of $C?$" :question/worked-solution "The parameter $C$ represents a horizontal shift of the function.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the function by factoring the horizontal stretch factor, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x+C) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $x+\\frac{C}{2}$ indicates that the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2(x+\\frac{C}{2}))$ is a horizontal translation of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x).$ Comparing the two graphs below allows us to determine the amount of this shift.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007410/assets/595222a0a6987c1fae1a7b245d2936eba08312357015cc6f78c66eb60f942707.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that our curve has been obtained by shifting $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)$ by $\\frac{5\\pi }{12}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ units to the right. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{C}{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<C<\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is in this interval, the value of $C$ is $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143671/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84355770-5926-5be6-9b9f-c13bb05599ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
